      "lineNbr": 93,
      "author": {
        "id": 1956258
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-09T22:04:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "memcmp will need zero array for comparison which has allocation cost. something like this can be done but I don\u0027t think it is really readable.\n\n```\nstatic int memvcmp(void *memory, unsigned char val, unsigned int size)\n{\n    unsigned char *mm \u003d (unsigned char*)memory;\n    return (*mm \u003d\u003d val) \u0026\u0026 memcmp(mm, mm + 1, size - 1) \u003d\u003d 0;\n}\n\n```",
      "parentUuid": "d651c55a_934591ff",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 93,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 93,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "d2a001a4762d18144ec6c9a743c3d26bb77b9638",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
